course: dictionary
lesson: 5607
title: Lifespan
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A lifespan is how long something lives, or how long it lasts. For a living thing, it is the time from its birth to its death. For a machine, it is how long it works before it wears out. «No red dwarf in the universe has yet died of old age, because the universe is far younger than their lifespans.» The universe is about 13.8 billion years old, so the red dwarfs have not yet reached the end of their lives.
explain: Look at the words around lifespan to get its meaning. Lifespan is often used with words like «average», «short» or «expected». An average lifespan is the usual amount of time, a short lifespan is not very long, and an expected lifespan is the time we think something will last.
explain: Lifespan is a noun, and you can write it as lifespans when you mean more than one. You can also write it as two words, life span, and both spellings are correct. Use it when you compare how long different things last, such as a mayfly and a dog.
fact: A lifespan is how long a living thing lives, or how long a thing lasts or works.
fact: A mayfly has a lifespan of about one day, and a mouse has a lifespan of about 2 years.
fact: A dog has a lifespan of about 12 years, and a human has a lifespan of about 80 years.
fact: The Greenland shark has a lifespan of hundreds of years, which makes it one of the longest-lived animals.
fact: «Average lifespan», «short lifespan» and «expected lifespan» are common phrases, and you can see them in science and maths.
exercise: «A mayfly's lifespan is only one day.» What does lifespan mean here? | How many friends someone has | How tall something grows | How fast something can run | *How long something lives or lasts
exercise: A mouse has a lifespan of about 2 years, a dog about 12 years, and a Greenland shark hundreds of years. Which animal has the longest lifespan? | Mayfly | Mouse | *Greenland shark | Dog
exercise: Which phrase is about a thing that does not last long? | A bright light | An average lifespan | A long walk | *A short lifespan
test: Maya's phone has a lifespan of about 4 years. What does lifespan tell us about the phone? | Who made the phone | How much the phone weighs | *How long the phone will last and work | The colour of the phone
test: A dog has a lifespan of about 12 years and a mouse has a lifespan of about 2 years. About how many years longer does a dog's lifespan last? | About 2 years | *About 10 years | About 80 years | About 14 years
exam: «No red dwarf in the universe has yet died of old age, because the universe is far younger than their lifespans.» What does this tell us? | The red dwarfs are exactly 13.8 billion years old | *The red dwarfs will last longer than the universe has existed so far | The red dwarfs are the same as a mayfly | The red dwarfs last only one day
